# ==================================================================
# Reference source archives
# ==================================================================
#
# tmp/ holds large source downloads that derived files are built from
# and that the repository does not need: the 12.8 MB 鄉鎮市區界線
# shapefile is re-downloadable from data.gov.tw dataset 7441, and what
# the project depends on is data/reference/districts.json and
# public/data/districts.geojson, both committed. See CLAUDE.md 4.1.
#
# This does not weaken the data/ rule below. data/ stays fully tracked;
# tmp/ is a separate staging area precisely so that everything under
# data/ can keep the invariant "if it is here, it is committed".
/tmp/

# ==================================================================
# Scratch notes and generated previews
# ==================================================================
#
# .notes/ holds prototypes, mock-ups and screenshots produced while
# working out a design: useful next to the code, worth nothing to a
# reader of the repository, and heavy (a full-page PNG runs to several
# hundred KB). Anything from here that turns out to be worth keeping
# gets described in DESIGN.md rather than committed as an image.
#
# The desktop client writes its own deliveries to "Claude outputs/";
# that name is ignored too so the folder cannot reappear and be swept
# in by git add -A.
/.notes/

# Tarball used to move the tree into a sandbox for a build check.
/_transfer.tgz
/Claude outputs/

# ==================================================================
# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED - do not "tidy up" the entries below.
# ==================================================================
#
# data/
#   The daily snapshot workflow commits data/raw/YYYY-MM-DD.csv.gz back
#   into the repo. If data/ were ignored the workflow would silently
#   store nothing, and the loss would only surface days later.
#   See CLAUDE.md 6.3.
#
# public/data/
#   Generated JSON / GeoJSON consumed by the frontend. GitHub Pages
#   serves it as a static asset. Committed on purpose so the Pages deploy
#   is decoupled from the Python pipeline: a broken pipeline leaves the
#   site up with slightly stale data instead of failing the deploy.
#   See CLAUDE.md 4.1.
#
# ==================================================================
